¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYe stand this day all of you before the LORD your God; your captains of your tribes, your elders, and your officers, with all the men of Israel,¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|your little ones, your wives, and thy stranger that is in thy camp, from the hewer of thy wood unto the drawer of thy water:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒthat thou shouldest enter into covenant with the LORD thy God, and into his oath, which the LORD thy God maketh with thee this day:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÆthat he may establish thee to day for a people unto himself, and that he may be unto thee a God, as he hath said unto thee, and as he hath sworn unto thy fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<Neither with you only do I make this covenant and this oath;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~but with him that standeth here with us this day before the LORD our God, and also with him that is not here with us this day:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙl(for ye know how we have dwelt in the land of Egypt; and how we came through the nations which ye passed by;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnand ye have seen their abominations, and their idols, wood and stone, silver and gold, which were among them:)¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙìlest there should be among you man, or woman, or family, or tribe, whose heart turneth away this day from the LORD our God, to go and serve the gods of these nations; lest there should be among you a root that beareth gall and wormwood;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËand it come to pass, when he heareth the words of this curse, that he bless himself in his heart, saying, I shall have peace, though I walk in the imagination of mine heart, to add drunkenness to thirst:¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙçthe LORD will not spare him, but then the anger of the LORD and his jealousy shall smoke against that man, and all the curses that are written in this book shall lie upon him, and the LORD shall blot out his name from under heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And the LORD shall separate him unto evil out of all the tribes of Israel, according to all the curses of the covenant that are written in this book of the law:¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙçso that the generation to come of your children that shall rise up after you, and the stranger that shall come from a far land, shall say, when they see the plagues of that land, and the sicknesses which the LORD hath laid upon it;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙüand that the whole land thereof is brimstone, and salt, and burning, that it is not sown, nor beareth, nor any grass groweth therein, like the overthrow of Sodom, and Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboim, which the LORD overthrew in his anger, and in his wrath:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxeven all nations shall say, Wherefore hath the LORD done thus unto this land? what meaneth the heat of this great anger?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªThen men shall say, Because they have forsaken the covenant of the LORD God of their fathers, which he made with them when he brought them forth out of the land of Egypt:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwfor they went and served other gods, and worshipped them, gods whom they knew not, and whom he had not given unto them:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwand the anger of the LORD was kindled against this land, to bring upon it all the curses that are written in this book:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand the LORD rooted them out of their land in anger, and in wrath, and in great indignation, and cast them into another land, as it is this day.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªThe secret things belong unto the LORD our God: but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever, that we may do all the words of this law.¦layout ªlast_verse